<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Configuration for AgentA11yService.

  ================== READ THIS FIRST: THE SERVICE DOES NOT WORK ==================

  Goal was to make WeChat expose its node tree without making the user run TalkBack
  or SelectToSpeak. It failed. Six variants were built, installed and measured, and
  EVERY one scored 0/3 while SelectToSpeak scored 3/3 under the identical procedure.

  The measurements, and what each ruled out:

    variant  what it declared                          WeChat
    -------  ----------------------------------------  ------
    ref      no service bound                          0/3   (0, 0, 0)
    ref      TalkBack                                  1/3   (0, 68, 0)
    ref      SelectToSpeak                             3/3   (68, 68, 68)
    v3.3     feedbackSpoken, canRetrieveWindowContent  0/3   bound OK, requestA11yBtn=false
    v3.4     + accessibilityFlags, feedbackAllMask     0/3   feedback became all-mask
    v3.5     every value copied from SelectToSpeak     0/3   verified in the XML resource
    v3.6     + FEEDBACK_GENERIC category in manifest   0/3   capabilities 1 -> 9
    v3.7     + setServiceInfo() at runtime             0/3   capabilities=9
    ctrl     SelectToSpeak, same script, same screen   3/3   (68, 68, 68)

  How SelectToSpeak's config was obtained, so this does not have to be redone: its
  manifest entry points at resource 0x7f18004a, which the resource table maps to
  res/9r.xml inside TalkBack's base.apk. Dumping that file gives the exact values this
  file now carries. They were copied, not guessed.

  What this leaves as the explanation: WeChat is most likely keying on the CLIENT's
  package name or signing identity, not on the accessibility configuration it declares.
  Everything declarable has been matched and it made no difference. That is a hypothesis,
  not a measurement: confirming it would mean reading WeChat's detection code, which has
  not been done.

  CONSEQUENCE: enabling this service achieves nothing. It is kept only as a record of a
  negative result. If the tree is needed from WeChat, the working option is a service the
  app already trusts: SelectToSpeak measured 3/3, at the cost of a floating button
  (requestA11yBtn=true). TalkBack works too but only 1/3 and it changes how taps are
  interpreted, which is worse.

  ============================== ATTRIBUTE NOTES ==============================

  The values below are SelectToSpeak's, reproduced exactly. Deliberately NOT included,
  because it is what draws the floating button:

      flagRequestAccessibilityButton (0x100)

  packageNames is intentionally absent here: it was present in v3.3 and v3.5, and its
  removal in v3.6 changed nothing, so it is not the trigger either.
-->
<accessibility-service xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:description="@string/a11y_service_description"
    android:summary="@string/a11y_service_summary"
    android:accessibilityEventTypes="typeViewClicked|typeNotificationStateChanged|typeWindowContentChanged|typeViewScrolled|typeWindowsChanged"
    android:accessibilityFeedbackType="feedbackSpoken|feedbackVisual"
    android:accessibilityFlags="flagDefault|flagReportViewIds|flagIncludeNotImportantViews|flagRequestEnhancedWebAccessibility|flagRequestFilterKeyEvents|flagRetrieveInteractiveWindows"
    android:canRetrieveWindowContent="true"
    android:canRequestFilterKeyEvents="true"
    android:notificationTimeout="0" />
